[gd_scene load_steps=32 format=3]

; ============================================================================
; MISTVALE PLAZA — THE FIRST PLAYABLE SEQUENCE
; ============================================================================
;
; THIS IS THE FIRST SCENE IN THE PROJECT THAT IS A GAME RATHER THAN AN INSTRUMENT.
; The combat sandbox is a measurement rig with a 24 m floor and a dummy on it; the
; region is a 660 m level-design review with a free-fly walker. Neither of them is
; a place a player is meant to arrive in. This one is.
;
; TWO STACKS, AND NOTHING ELSE IN THE FILE.
;
;   1. THE WORLD — the ART line's existing region layers, unchanged: Terrain for
;      the ground and its collision, Land for roads and water, HeroEnvironment for
;      the composed landmarks, Town for the houses and Landmarks for the Bell Tower
;      and the Guild Hall. Nothing here duplicates any of them, and the plaza's own
;      dressing (the apron, the stalls, the alley) is built by `mistvale_plaza.gd`
;      on top of them.
;
;      `Ascent` and `Flora` are deliberately ABSENT. Ascent is 160 m of mountain
;      path the player cannot reach from this square, and Flora is the single most
;      expensive builder in the project, spent on a valley that is behind the
;      houses from every position the first playable ever puts the camera in.
;
;   2. THE COMBAT BACKBONE — copied from `CombatSandbox.tscn` because it is not
;      optional. `CombatController._ready()` reaches for `CombatScreenFX`,
;      `TimeEffectManager` and `IaidoDirector` with a bare `get_node()`, and
;      `IaidoDirector` reaches for seven more, so a world that mounts a Player
;      without them throws on the first frame and on every pause thereafter. They
;      are mounted here rather than guarded for, because guarding them would mean
;      editing the combat line to suit a new scene.
;
; WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. `CombatHUD` — §20 asks the first playable to build
; its HUD up as the story earns it, and the combat HUD is a full-fat overlay with
; three resource bars, a spell wheel and a spell banner. `StoryUI` shows the one bar
; that matters (health) and only from the first fight. `ArenaDressing`,
; `WindProps`, `MovementLane`, `ChainLab` and `ExecutionLab` are all sandbox stages.
;
; EVERY ACTOR POSITION IS SET BY THE SCRIPT, NOT BY THIS FILE. XZ comes from five
; constants at the top of `mistvale_plaza.gd` and Y from `MistvaleHeights`, so the
; transforms below are placeholders that exist only so the scene opens sensibly in
; the editor.

